   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(24, 7))\n",
    "sns.swarmplot(data=X, x=\"make\", y=y, size=3, ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set(title=\"Car maker vs. price — swarm plot\", xlabel=\"Car maker\", ylabel=\"Price\")\n",
    "ax.tick_params(axis=\"x\", labelrotation=45)\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "jUBTxP0vBJNd"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Note:** This plot can be slow and hard to read for very large datasets, but for our cleaned dataset of 159 cars, it works well."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "L9rgvA43bM9t"
   },
   "source": [
    "Now let us try to learn a bit more about the various features in our dataset. One of the features is **Horsepower**, used to describe the power that an engine is capable of producing. A sensible assumption could be that Sport car companies like Porsche would have more cars with higher horsepowers. Lets check if this is actually true ..."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 494
    },
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-10T08:05:44.872635Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-10T08:05:44.871636Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-10T08:05:45.778070Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-10T08:05:45.778070Z"
    },
    "id": "fHNWk2yW4oba",
    "outputId": "e6f930df-2335-4b2f-81c3-2d5cd7e66634"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 2400x700 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "horsepower = pd.to_numeric(X[\"horsepower\"])\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(24, 7))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x=X[\"make\"], y=horsepower, hue=X[\"make\"], palette=\"Set3\", dodge=False, legend=False, ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set(title=\"Car maker vs. horsepower\", xlabel=\"Car maker\", ylabel=\"Horsepower\")\n",
    "ax.tick_params(axis=\"x\", labelrotation=45)\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "9LpO4EYHvrOe"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Horsepower and price\n",
    "\n",
    "The scatterplot and regression line show a positive relationship: cars with higher horsepower tend to have higher prices in this cleaned sample. The Pearson correlation is about **0.760**, a strong positive linear association, although points do not fall exactly on a line and correlation does not imply that horsepower alone determines price.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 490
    },
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-10T08:05:45.784497Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-10T08:05:45.784497Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.113457Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.111444Z"
    },
    "id": "svOacOwc7_F7",
    "outputId": "25ebe172-f810-4c2b-e261-8dfa061b863c"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 700x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "horsepower = pd.to_numeric(X[\"horsepower\"])\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(x=horsepower, y=y, color=\"red\", alpha=0.75, ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set(title=\"Horsepower vs. price\", xlabel=\"Horsepower\", ylabel=\"Price\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Yemgn7lUw1Pd"
   },
   "source": [
    "A better way of plotting these correlations is using a **Jointplot** instead of a simple scatter plot. The jointplot displays a relationship between 2 variables (bivariate) as well as 1D profiles (univariate) in the margins.\n",
    "\n",
    "I have also used the parameter \"reg\" which fits a regression line through the points making the correlation sign apparent. A line with positive slope would indicate a postiive correlation and vice versa. A line parallel to x-axis would indicate no correlation between the 2 variables (implying independence)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 618
    },
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.119158Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.118161Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.914818Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-10T08:05:46.912295Z"
    },
    "id": "VjCeYDT5-MW0",
    "outputId": "ccc8e140-fd60-42d4-e4f8-ce01be5c0434"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Pearson correlation (horsepower, price): 0.760\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 700x700 with 3 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "horsepower = pd.to_numeric(X[\"horsepower\"])\n",
    "g = sns.jointplot(x=horsepower, y=y, kind=\"reg\", color=\"green\", height=7)\n",
    "g.set_axis_labels(\"Horsepower\", \"Price\")\n",
    "g.fig.suptitle(\"Horsepower and price: joint distribution\", y=1.02)\n",
    "print(f\"Pearson correlation (horsepower, price): {horsepower.corr(y):.3f}\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
