   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "S4iu9_wPCodR"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Interpretation of highway-MPG vs. price:**\n",
    "\n",
    "The regression line slopes downward. In this cleaned sample, the Pearson correlation is about **-0.720**, indicating a strong negative linear association: cars with higher highway fuel economy tend to be less expensive. This is a pattern, not a rule for every car, and it does not establish that fuel economy causes a lower price.\n"
   ]
  },
